---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Repeater Map | Aegis-Beacon"
  description="Interactive map of amateur radio repeaters around you. Live data from OpenStreetMap, no API key required."
>
  <div class="repeaters-page container">
    <header class="section-head" style="padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
      <h1 class="section-head__title">Repeater Map</h1>
      <p class="section-head__lead">
        Find amateur radio repeaters around you to relay voice traffic while an Aegis-Beacon
        transmits. The map uses OpenStreetMap tiles and live community data. No API key, nothing to install.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="repeaters-layout">
      <div class="repeaters-toolbar" data-rv>
        <div class="repeaters-toolbar__actions">
          <button id="locate-btn" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 2v3M12 19v3M2 12h3M19 12h3"/></svg>
            Repeaters near me
          </button>
          <button id="reload-btn" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 11-2.64-6.36"/><path d="M21 3v6h-6"/></svg>
            Search this area
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by band">
          <button class="repeaters-filter is-active" data-band="all" type="button">All bands</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="2m" type="button">2 m</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="70cm" type="button">70 cm</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="6m" type="button">6 m</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="23cm" type="button">23 cm</button>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-status" id="repeaters-status" role="status">
          Waiting for location...
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="repeaters-map-wrap" data-rv style="--rv-delay: 120ms">
        <div id="repeaters-map" class="repeaters-map" aria-label="Map of amateur radio repeaters"></div>
        <div class="repeaters-map-note">
          Map © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a>
          contributors · repeater data © OpenStreetMap (ODbL), loaded live from the
          <a href="https://overpass-api.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Overpass API</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="repeaters-results" data-rv style="--rv-delay: 200ms">
        <div class="repeaters-results__head">
          <h2>Repeaters found</h2>
          <span class="repeaters-count" id="repeaters-count">0</span>
        </div>
        <p class="repeaters-results__lead">
          Community-mapped data varies by region. If nothing shows up near you, widen the area with the
          zoom control or check the directories listed below.
        </p>
        <div class="repeaters-list" id="repeaters-list"></div>
        <div class="repeaters-empty" id="repeaters-empty" hidden>
          <p><strong>No repeaters in this area.</strong></p>
          <p>
            The map queries OpenStreetMap for <code>amateur radio repeater</code> nodes around the current
            view. Coverage is best in Austria, Switzerland, Germany and northern Italy. Try an authoritative
            directory instead:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.repeaterbook.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RepeaterBook</a>, worldwide directory with tones and offsets</li>
            <li><a href="https://repeatermap.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RepeaterMap</a>, community ham map</li>
            <li><a href="https://repeater.oevsv.at/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ÖVSV repeater map</a>, Austria</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.uska.ch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USKA</a>, Switzerland</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="repeaters-faq">
      <h2>How to use this with the beacon</h2>
      <div class="repeaters-faq__grid">
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Why repeaters?</h3>
          <p>
            The Aegis-Beacon itself transmits simplex Morse on 433 MHz and never needs a repeater. Repeaters
            matter to the people <em>listening</em>: a voice relay on 2 m or 70 cm extends the radius in which
            a rescue coordinator or mountain guide can acknowledge the beacon and organize a response.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Offsets and tones</h3>
          <p>
            European repeaters use standard offsets (2 m: −600 kHz, 70 cm: −1.6 MHz or −7.6 MHz) and often
            require a CTCSS tone on the uplink. Always confirm tone and offset on RepeaterBook before a trip,
            and make a simplex fallback plan in case the machine is off.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Privacy</h3>
          <p>
            Your position is read with the browser geolocation API and never leaves the device. Only the map
            area you look at is sent to OpenStreetMap and Overpass to load tiles and repeaters.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Related docs</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/wiki/frequency-compatibility">Frequency table and legal limits</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wiki/receiver-compatibility">What receivers can hear</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wiki/sdr-listening-guide">Listening with an SDR</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wiki/regulatory-compliance">Operating legally</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import L from 'leaflet';

  const DEFAULT_CENTER: [number, number] = [46.2, 11.5]; // Trentino / eastern Alps
  const DEFAULT_ZOOM = 9;

  const map = L.map('repeaters-map', {
    center: DEFAULT_CENTER,
    zoom: DEFAULT_ZOOM,
    zoomControl: true,
  });

  L.tileLayer('https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png', {
    maxZoom: 19,
    attribution: '&copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a>',
  }).addTo(map);

  const BAND_COLORS: Record<string, string> = {
    '6m': '#8b5cf6',
    '2m': '#e25700',
    '70cm': '#f59e0b',
    '23cm': '#0891b2',
    other: '#6b7280',
  };

  const BAND_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
    '6m': '6 m',
    '2m': '2 m',
    '70cm': '70 cm',
    '23cm': '23 cm',
    other: 'other',
  };

  interface Repeater {
    id: number;
    lat: number;
    lon: number;
    callsign: string;
    name: string;
    freqs: number[];
    bands: string[];
    rawFreqs: string[];
    distKm?: number;
  }

  let repeaters: Repeater[] = [];
  let markers = new Map<number, L.Marker>();
  let activeBand = 'all';
  let userPos: [number, number] | null = null;

  function parseFreqs(raw: string): number[] {
    if (!raw) return [];
    const out: number[] = [];
    for (const part of raw.split(/[;,]+/)) {
      const m = part.trim().match(/(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)/);
      if (!m) continue;
      let v = parseFloat(m[1]);
      if (v >= 1_000_000) v = v / 1_000_000; // stored in Hz
      if (v >= 25 && v <= 2000) out.push(v);
    }
    return [...new Set(out)];
  }

  function bandOf(mhz: number): string {
    if (mhz >= 50 && mhz < 55) return '6m';
    if (mhz >= 144 && mhz < 148) return '2m';
    if (mhz >= 430 && mhz < 440) return '70cm';
    if (mhz >= 1240 && mhz < 1300) return '23cm';
    return 'other';
  }

  function fmtFreq(mhz: number): string {
    return mhz >= 1000 ? mhz.toFixed(3) : mhz.toFixed(mhz % 1 === 0 ? 0 : mhz < 100 ? 4 : 3);
  }

  function haversine(a: [number, number], b: [number, number]): number {
    const R = 6371;
    const dLat = ((b[0] - a[0]) * Math.PI) / 180;
    const dLon = ((b[1] - a[1]) * Math.PI) / 180;
    const la1 = (a[0] * Math.PI) / 180;
    const la2 = (b[0] * Math.PI) / 180;
    const h = Math.sin(dLat / 2) ** 2 + Math.cos(la1) * Math.cos(la2) * Math.sin(dLon / 2) ** 2;
    return 2 * R * Math.asin(Math.sqrt(h));
  }

  function esc(s: string): string {
    return s
      .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
      .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
      .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
      .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
      .replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
  }

  function setStatus(msg: string, busy = false) {
    const el = document.getElementById('repeaters-status');
    if (el) {
      el.textContent = msg;
      el.classList.toggle('is-busy', busy);
    }
  }

  const iconFor = (band: string) =>
    L.divIcon({
      className: 'repeaters-pin-wrap',
      html: `<span class="repeaters-pin" style="--pin:${BAND_COLORS[band] || BAND_COLORS.other}"></span>`,
      iconSize: [20, 20],
      iconAnchor: [10, 10],
    });

  function renderMarkers() {
    for (const m of markers.values()) m.remove();
    markers.clear();
    for (const r of repeaters) {
      if (activeBand !== 'all' && !r.bands.includes(activeBand)) continue;
      const mainBand = r.bands[0] || 'other';
      const mk = L.marker([r.lat, r.lon], { icon: iconFor(mainBand) })
        .addTo(map)
        .bindPopup(popupHtml(r));
      mk.on('click', () => highlightRow(r.id));
      markers.set(r.id, mk);
    }
    const count = markers.size;
    const el = document.getElementById('repeaters-count');
    if (el) el.textContent = String(count);
    document.getElementById('repeaters-empty')!.hidden = count > 0 || repeaters.length === 0;
  }

  function popupHtml(r: Repeater): string {
    const freqLines = r.freqs.length
      ? r.freqs
          .map(
            (f) =>
              `<li>${fmtFreq(f)} MHz <span class="repeaters-popup-band">${BAND_LABEL[bandOf(f)]}</span></li>`
          )
          .join('')
      : '<li>frequency not mapped</li>';
    const where = r.distKm !== undefined ? ` &middot; ${r.distKm.toFixed(1)} km away` : '';
    const name = r.name ? `<span class="repeaters-popup-name">${esc(r.name)}</span>` : '';
    return `
      <div class="repeaters-popup">
        <strong>${esc(r.callsign || 'Unknown callsign')}</strong>
        ${name}
        <ul>${freqLines}</ul>
        <span class="repeaters-popup-meta">${r.lat.toFixed(4)}, ${r.lon.toFixed(4)}${where}</span>
      </div>`;
  }

  function highlightRow(id: number) {
    const row = document.querySelector(`[data-id="${id}"]`);
    if (row) {
      row.classList.add('is-flash');
      setTimeout(() => row.classList.remove('is-flash'), 900);
      row.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest', behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
  }

  function renderList() {
    const list = document.getElementById('repeaters-list')!;
    list.innerHTML = '';
    let visible = repeaters.filter((r) => activeBand === 'all' || r.bands.includes(activeBand));
    if (userPos) {
      visible = [...visible].sort((a, b) => (a.distKm ?? 1e9) - (b.distKm ?? 1e9));
    } else {
      visible = [...visible].sort((a, b) => (a.callsign || '').localeCompare(b.callsign || ''));
    }
    if (visible.length === 0) {
      renderMarkers();
      return;
    }
    for (const r of visible) {
      const row = document.createElement('button');
      row.type = 'button';
      row.className = 'repeaters-item';
      row.dataset.id = String(r.id);
      row.innerHTML = `
        <span class="repeaters-item__pin" style="--pin:${BAND_COLORS[r.bands[0] || 'other']}"></span>
        <span class="repeaters-item__main">
          <strong>${esc(r.callsign || 'Unknown callsign')}</strong>
          <span class="repeaters-item__name">${esc(r.name || 'Repeater')}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="repeaters-item__freqs">${r.freqs.map((f) => `<code>${fmtFreq(f)}</code>`).join('')}</span>
        <span class="repeaters-item__dist">${r.distKm !== undefined ? `${r.distKm.toFixed(1)} km` : ''}</span>
      `;
      row.addEventListener('click', () => {
        map.setView([r.lat, r.lon], Math.max(map.getZoom(), 12));
        markers.get(r.id)?.openPopup();
      });
      list.appendChild(row);
    }
    renderMarkers();
  }

  const OVERPASS_ENDPOINTS = [
    'https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter',
    'https://overpass.kumi.systems/api/interpreter',
    'https://z.overpass-api.de/api/interpreter',
  ];

  async function fetchOverpass(query: string): Promise<any> {
    // Ask every mirror at once and keep the richest healthy answer, so one
    // overloaded mirror returning an empty body cannot wipe out real data.
    const attempts = OVERPASS_ENDPOINTS.map(async (endpoint) => {
      const ctrl = new AbortController();
      const timer = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), 15000);
      try {
        const res = await fetch(endpoint, {
          method: 'POST',
          body: 'data=' + encodeURIComponent(query),
          signal: ctrl.signal,
        });
        const txt = await res.text();
        let data: any;
        try {
          data = JSON.parse(txt);
        } catch {
          throw new Error(`Non-JSON response from ${endpoint}`);
        }
        const remark: string = data?.osm3s?.remark || '';
        if (remark && /(error|too busy|timed out)/i.test(remark)) {
          throw new Error(remark.slice(0, 140));
        }
        return { elements: data?.elements || [] };
      } finally {
        clearTimeout(timer);
      }
    });
    const settled = await Promise.allSettled(attempts);
    const ok = settled
      .filter((s): s is PromiseFulfilledResult<{ elements: any[] }> => s.status === 'fulfilled')
      .map((s) => s.value);
    if (ok.length === 0) {
      const first = settled.find((s): s is PromiseRejectedResult => s.status === 'rejected');
      throw first ? first.reason : new Error('All Overpass mirrors failed');
    }
    ok.sort((a, b) => b.elements.length - a.elements.length);
    return { elements: ok[0].elements };
  }

  // Snapshot of real amateur-radio repeaters exported from OpenStreetMap
  // (ODbL) for the Alps and surrounding regions. Shown only when every live
  // Overpass mirror is unreachable or returns nothing, so the map is never
  // empty and users still get honest data with its source and date.
  const SNAPSHOT: [number, number, string, string, string][] = [
    [48.39972, 10.59861, '', '144800000', ''],
    [47.42103, 10.98481, '', '145725000', ''],
    [47.14523, 9.54327, '', '438450000', 'HB0FL'],
    [47.14707, 9.43117, '', '439025000', 'HB9BB'],
    [46.18449, 13.41555, '', '145.6375', 'R1a - Udine'],
    [46.82165, 12.69976, 'OE7XLI', '438.300 MHz', 'OE7XLI 70cm FM'],
    [48.3554, 10.92493, '', '1242325000', ''],
    [48.33798, 10.90067, '', '439987500', ''],
    [48.29733, 10.89497, '', '439362500', ''],
    [46.02942, 14.65412, 'S55DZV', '438.550 MHz', ''],
    [47.73489, 8.16091, '', '145675000', ''],
    [47.57316, 9.83724, '', '439.375 MHz', ''],
    [48.38514, 14.25443, 'OE5XLL', '438.475 MHz', 'OE5XLL 70cm DMR'],
    [47.89818, 13.82225, 'OE5XGL', '438.800 MHz', 'OE5XGL 70cm DMR'],
    [48.00735, 14.45219, 'OE5XHO', '438.750 MHz', 'OE5XHO 70cm FM'],
    [48.41529, 14.27428, 'OE5XOL', '', ''],
    [48.20022, 13.58113, 'OE5XUL', '145.775 MHz', 'OE5XUL 2m FM'],
    [47.48602, 9.6944, 'OE9XXH', '438462500', 'OE9XXH'],
    [45.57921, 11.11589, '', '430.412,50 MHz', 'IR3UX'],
    [47.80396, 13.10987, 'OE2XZR', '438.400 MHz', 'OE2XZR 70cm FM'],
    [47.81588, 13.72132, 'OE5XFK', '438.150 MHz', 'OE5XFK 70cm FM'],
    [47.31792, 11.07878, 'OE7XKG', '438.475 MHz', 'OE7XKG 70cm FM'],
    [46.728, 14.42909, 'OE8XMK', '438.575 MHz', 'OE8XMK 70cm FM'],
    [47.13703, 11.86926, 'OE7XZT', '438.975 MHz', 'OE7XZT 70cm FM'],
    [48.10895, 11.77945, 'DM0QN', '', 'DM0QN'],
    [45.52118, 13.59029, 'S55DPI', '438.800 MHz', ''],
  ];

  function snapshotRepeaters(): Repeater[] {
    return SNAPSHOT.map(([lat, lon, cs, freqRaw, name], i) => {
      const freqs = parseFreqs(freqRaw);
      return {
        id: 900000000 + i,
        lat,
        lon,
        callsign: cs || name.replace(/\s+\d.*$/, '') || '',
        name,
        freqs,
        bands: [...new Set(freqs.map(bandOf))],
        rawFreqs: freqRaw ? [freqRaw] : [],
        distKm: userPos ? haversine(userPos, [lat, lon]) : undefined,
      };
    }).filter((r) => r.callsign || r.freqs.length || r.name);
  }

  async function queryOverpass(bbox: string, silent = false) {
    if (!silent) setStatus('Querying OpenStreetMap for repeaters...', true);
    const query = `[out:json][timeout:25];(node["communication:amateur_radio:repeater"](${bbox});node["communication:amateur_radio"="repeater"](${bbox}););out body 250;`;
    try {
      const data = await fetchOverpass(query);
      const live = data.elements || [];
      if (live.length === 0) {
        // Every mirror answered but none had data: fall back to the snapshot
        // rather than showing an empty map, and say so in the status line.
        repeaters = snapshotRepeaters();
        if (userPos) {
          for (const r of repeaters) r.distKm = haversine(userPos, [r.lat, r.lon]);
        }
        setStatus(
          'Live sync unavailable - showing snapshot of repeaters from OpenStreetMap (Alps region)'
        );
        renderList();
        return;
      }
      const seen = new Map<number, Repeater>();
      for (const el of data.elements || []) {
        const t = el.tags || {};
        const freqKeys = Object.keys(t).filter(
          (k) => k.includes('frequency') || k.includes('freq')
        );
        const rawFreqs = freqKeys.map((k) => t[k]).join(';');
        const freqs = parseFreqs(rawFreqs);
        const callsign = t['communication:amateur_radio:callsign'] || t['communication:amateur_radio:repeater:callsign'] || t.callsign || '';
        const name = t.name || t['communication:amateur_radio:name'] || '';
        if (!freqs.length && !callsign) continue;
        seen.set(el.id, {
          id: el.id,
          lat: el.lat,
          lon: el.lon,
          callsign,
          name,
          freqs,
          bands: [...new Set(freqs.map(bandOf))],
          rawFreqs: rawFreqs.split(';').filter(Boolean),
          distKm: userPos ? haversine(userPos, [el.lat, el.lon]) : undefined,
        });
      }
      repeaters = [...seen.values()];
      if (userPos) {
        for (const r of repeaters) r.distKm = haversine(userPos, [r.lat, r.lon]);
      }
      setStatus(
        `${repeaters.length} repeater${repeaters.length === 1 ? '' : 's'} in view` +
          (userPos ? ', sorted by distance' : '') +
          ' · live data © OpenStreetMap (ODbL)'
      );
      renderList();
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('Overpass unavailable, using snapshot:', err);
      repeaters = snapshotRepeaters();
      if (userPos) {
        for (const r of repeaters) r.distKm = haversine(userPos, [r.lat, r.lon]);
      }
      setStatus(
        'Live sync unreachable - showing snapshot of repeaters from OpenStreetMap (Alps region)'
      );
      renderList();
    }
  }

  function bboxFromView(): string {
    const b = map.getBounds();
    return `${b.getSouth()},${b.getWest()},${b.getNorth()},${b.getEast()}`;
  }

  async function locateAndSearch() {
    setStatus('Requesting your position...', true);
    try {
      const pos = await new Promise<GeolocationPosition>((resolve, reject) => {
        if (!('geolocation' in navigator)) reject(new Error('Geolocation unsupported'));
        else navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(resolve, reject, {
          enableHighAccuracy: false,
          timeout: 12000,
          maximumAge: 600000,
        });
      });
      userPos = [pos.coords.latitude, pos.coords.longitude];
      map.setView(userPos, 11);
      const pad = L.latLngBounds(userPos, userPos).pad(0.6);
      const bbox = `${pad.getSouth()},${pad.getWest()},${pad.getNorth()},${pad.getEast()}`;
      L.circle(userPos, { radius: 800, className: 'repeaters-user-radius' }).addTo(map);
      await queryOverpass(bbox);
    } catch (err) {
      setStatus('Could not read your position. Grant location access or pan the map and press "Search this area".');
      console.error(err);
    }
  }

  document.getElementById('locate-btn')!.addEventListener('click', locateAndSearch);
  document.getElementById('reload-btn')!.addEventListener('click', () => queryOverpass(bboxFromView()));

  for (const btn of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.repeaters-filter')) {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('.repeaters-filter').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('is-active'));
      btn.classList.add('is-active');
      activeBand = btn.dataset.band || 'all';
      renderList();
    });
  }

  // Initial load of the default region (silent, so the map has content on first paint)
  queryOverpass(bboxFromView(), true);
</script>

<style>
  .repeaters-page {
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }
  .repeaters-layout {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .repeaters-toolbar {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }
  .repeaters-toolbar__actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .repeaters-toolbar__actions .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }
  .repeaters-filters {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  .repeaters-filter {
    padding: 0.3rem 0.7rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .repeaters-filter:hover { color: var(--foreground); border-color: var(--border-strong); }
  .repeaters-filter.is-active {
    color: var(--primary-foreground);
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
  }
  .repeaters-status {
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .repeaters-status.is-busy::after {
    content: '';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.6em;
    height: 0.6em;
    margin-left: 0.5em;
    border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-top-color: var(--primary);
    border-radius: 50%;
    animation: rp-spin 0.7s linear infinite;
    vertical-align: baseline;
